==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|back|ing}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbæk.ɪŋ(ɡ)/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-backing.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ækɪŋ|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# [[support|Support]], especially [[financial]].
#: {{ux|en|It's a volunteer organization that works with '''backing''' from the city and a few grants.}}
# A [[liner]] or other [[material]] added [[behind]] or [[underneath]].
#: {{ux|en|The cardboard '''backing''' gives the notebook a little extra stiffness.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1959|month=October|author=Norman Jones|title=The Manchester Ship Canal Railway|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=495|text=In general, the locomotives are painted dark green; the numberplates are brass, with a red '''backing''', and are usually carried on the tank side.}}
# {{lb|en|television|film}} A [[backdrop]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2013|author=Gerald Millerson|title=TV Scenic Design|page=134
|passage=The simplest and cheapest answer is to introduce a scenic '''backing''' of some kind, a backdrop, a drape, some flats to restrict the shot and obscure whatever is outside.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} [[musician|Musicians]] and [[vocalist]]s who support the main [[performer]].
# The mounting of a horse or other animal.
# The action of putting something back; a switching into reverse.

